      "message": "hexdigit() is used only by %h, which moved into %ph, which is inside #ifndef NO_UINT64_SUPPORT. So I get an unused function error on hexdigit() if CONFIG_DEBUG_PRINTF is set.\n\nThis is a functional change. The boards that set CONFIG_DEBUG_PRINTF are chell_pd, chocodile_vpdmcu, glados_pd, minimuffin, oak_pd, and zinger. The prints I see using %h that might be included by these boards are in spi_commands.c, i2c_master.c, host_command.c, trng.c, and vboot_hash.c.\n\nMaybe I need to try and refactor %h into a subroutine, and then figure out some more ugly ifdefs to stick in there so that %h still works if CONFIG_DEBUG_PRINTF is set. Or maybe this isn\u0027t worth it... not sure.",
